{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Elohim called the light Day.</b> Six things did HaShem name, for there was no man to name them, and they are: light, darkness, heavens, earth, seas, and man. Rabbi Elazar said: HaShem does not attach His name to harm but only to good, for it is written, 'And Elohim called the light Day,' but 'and the darkness Elohim called <b>night</b>' is not written." "<b>And the darkness.</b> That was already mentioned above. 'And it was evening and it was <b>morning' — even though the darkness was created from the first hour of night, he goes back and says, adjacent to the darkening, <b>and it was evening and it was morning</b>, that is, he goes back and includes all at once the entire work of the first day, and likewise on the other days.</b>" "<b>One day.</b> Rashi: according to the order of the language of the parashah, etc. — that is, the day of the Sole One of the world, who is called One; it was a day when there was nothing else in the world but Him, that is, the day belonged to Him alone and not to another. Another interpretation: according to its plain sense, it should not have written 'first day' but 'one day,' because it is not the way to call anything 'first' for a singular matter, and upon the completion of this day the other days had not yet been created."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:18:44.884396194Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}